Selmie decided to step down as a pro [[Shield Surfing|shield surfer]] and teach the next generation.<ref>{{Cite|I left the pro side of shield surfing behind to help the next generation step up, using this lodge as a teaching center.|Selmie|TotK}}</ref> As the [[Blizzard]] rages over [[Hebra Mountains]], she waits it out with her pupils [[Russ]] and [[Fin]].<ref>{{Cite|But shield surfing in this weather is nearly impossible to do safely. So I've put off teaching my students until the blizzard stops.|Selmie|TotK}}</ref> As [[Link]] visits their [[Selmie's Spot|cabin]] in such extreme weather, she assumes he is also a shield surfer and wants to learn from her.<ref>{{Cite|You startled me. How'd you make it all the way here in the blizzard? Are you a shield surfer too? Must be!|Selmie|TotK}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Oh, hey. I'm starting to think you came here to study shield surfing from me. Am I right?|Selmie|TotK}}</ref> When he confirms this, she declines taking on another student as her current ones would not receive as much training as they deserve.<ref>{{Cite|I've got to train the two students I have now before I can take on more. It'd be unfair to them to take on a third. |Selmie|TotK}}</ref> If he asks again she commends his attitude, but declines nonetheless.<ref>{{Cite|Heh. I like your attitude, asking again. Becoming a great shield surfer takes passion and commitment.|Selmie|TotK}}</ref> Should Link ask her what Shield Surfing is, she explains to him the basic idea of it.<ref>{{Cite|OK, here's the basic idea behind shield surfing... Take your favorite shield and turn it into a way to slide down snowy mountains with grace!|Selmie|TotK}}</ref> She also offers him a resting spot in the cabin and asks him to return once the Blizzard ends.<ref>{{Cite|It's dangerous around here in the blizzard. Feel free to rest in the lodge before you head out. And return here to show me your shield-surfing skills after this blizzard finally ends.|Selmie|TotK}}</ref>

